[2026-03-14T20:06:01.903Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01YHYXK2eopEniuZzWJtMLMu","type":"tool_result","content":"1803-#### Test: Creating a project and then opening modal again resets fields\n1804-- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, has just created a project via the modal\n1805-- **Action**: User clicks \"Create Project\" button again to open the modal\n1806-- **Expected**: All fields are reset to their defaults (Name is empty, Description is empty, Status is default, Lead is unset, Target date is unset, Teams is unset). No data from the previous creation persists in the form.\n1807-\n1808-#### Test: Created project appears immediately in the project list\n1809-- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, viewing `/projects` with 2 existing projects\n1810-- **Action**: User creates a new project \"API v3\" via the create project modal\n1811-- **Expected**: The project list now shows 3 projects, including the newly created \"API v3\". The new project appears without requiring a page refresh.\n1812-\n1813-#### Test: Create project modal Lead selector can be used multiple times\n1814-- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, create project modal is open\n1815-- **Action**: User selects \"Alice\" as lead, then clicks the lead selector again and changes to \"Bob\"\n1816-- **Expected**: The lead is updated to \"Bob\". The selector works correctly on repeated use. Only one lead can be selected at a time.\n1817-\n1818-#### Test: Create project modal Teams selector can be toggled multiple times\n1819-- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, create project modal is open\n1820-- **Action**: User selects \"Engineering\", then also selects \"Design\", then deselects \"Engineering\"\n1821-- **Expected**: Only \"Design\" remains selected. The multi-select works correctly through multiple toggle interactions.\n1822-\n1823:## Project Detail Page (`/project/:projectId`)\n1824-\n1825-**Components**: ProjectHeader, ProjectIssuesTab, ProjectOverviewTab\n1826-\n1827-### ProjectHeader\n1828-\n1829-#### Test: Project header renders all fields for an existing project\n1830-- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, viewing `/project/1`. Project \"Auth Rewrite\" exists with status \"In Progress\", lead \"Jane Doe\", target date 2026-04-15, and 10 issues (6 completed).\n1831-- **Expected**: The header displays the project name \"Auth Rewrite\" as an inline-editable text field. A status badge shows \"In Progress\" with appropriate styling. A progress bar shows 60% completion (6/10 issues). The target date \"Apr 15, 2026\" is displayed and inline-editable. The lead shows \"Jane Doe\" with avatar and is inline-editable.\n1832-\n1833-#### Test: Inline edit project name\n1834-- **Initial state**: User is viewing `/project/1`. Project name is \"Auth Rewrite\".\n1835-- **Action**: User clicks on the project name text, clears it, types \"Auth Rewrite v2\", and presses Enter or clicks away to confirm.\n1836-- **Expected**: The project name updates to \"Auth Rewrite v2\". The change is persisted to the database. An activity entry is created recording the name change.\n1837-\n1838-#### Test: Inline edit project name — cancel edit\n1839-- **Initial state**: User is viewing `/project/1`. Project name is \"Auth Rewrite\".\n1840-- **Action**: User clicks on the project name, types \"Draft Name\", then presses Escape.\n1841-- **Expected**: The project name reverts to \"Auth Rewrite\". No change is persisted.\n1842-\n1843-#### Test: Inline edit project name — validation rejects empty name"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01E2WFvEvPtdvDc7MyNoxSLV","session_id":"397be737-9668-41d0-bc33-0426ddb64020","uuid":"18238943-d4bf-4867-b1e1-db29447ab5d6"}
